From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: support a side fingerprint sensor on the left edge

SideFpsSensorInteractor places the side fingerprint indicator from the
sensor location that the fingerprint HAL reports in the display's default
orientation. It knows two placements: a horizontal sensor on the top edge
(sensorLocationY == 0, sensorLocationX is where it starts) and a vertical
sensor on the right edge (sensorLocationY is where it starts,
sensorLocationX is not used). A power key on the left edge in the default
orientation cannot be described, and the indicator ends up on the right
edge. This is the case on a tablet whose display reports landscape as its
natural orientation while the power key is on the left side.

Add config_sideFpsSensorOnLeftEdge, false by default. When a device sets
it, a vertical sensor is on the left edge. Such a sensor sits where a
right-edge sensor at the mirrored position (displayHeight -
sensorLocationY - length) sits with the display turned a further 180
degrees, so the interactor and the indicator's view rotation reuse the
right-edge placement with the rotation turned by 180 degrees. The
indicator asset is the same for opposite rotations and needs no change.
Devices that do not set the option behave as before.

SideFpsProgressBarViewModel, used only with config_restToUnlockSupported,
still assumes the right edge. The side fingerprint artwork in
BiometricPrompt and in Settings' enrollment screen is chosen from the
rotation alone and keeps showing the key on the right.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
